    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0536" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1199/218a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-08-26T13:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1936—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. Please deliver the following message to Stoppani from Rogers: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I am designating Mr. Leo Pasvolsky<anchor n="8a" xml:id="d370-f1"/> as
                            alternate to myself for the next meeting of the Economic Committee. We
                            will both be in attendance. I understand and trust this is agreeable to
                            you and to the Committee.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d370-f1" n="8a" xml:id="d370-f1-content">
                <p>Economic Analyst in the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
